.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH powerlinux-doctor 1  "PowerLinux 0.1.0" "PowerLinux Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
powerlinux\-doctor \- Check that everything PowerLinux needs is installed and set up
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpowerlinux doctor\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check that everything PowerLinux needs is installed and set up
.PP
Checks the helper programs, OCR language data, desktop portals, clipboard tools, the background service and hotkeys, then prints the install command for anything missing on this distro.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB✓\fR
In place.
.TP
\fB✗\fR
Missing, and the feature does not work without it.
.TP
\fB–\fR
Missing or off, but the feature still works in a limited way.
.PP
Install commands use the package manager of the running distribution (apt, dnf, pacman or zypper), detected from /etc/os\-release.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
0 when nothing required is missing, 1 otherwise, so it can be used in scripts.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBpowerlinux\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
